r reeves  to complete the final film in his planet  of the apes reboot trilogy 2017's war  for the planet of the apes affleck had  left the project reeves said to the  times i think ben was just evaluating  what he wanted to do and it wasn't what  i think he had fallen in love with in  terms of playing that character in the  first place but his departure definitely  affected the future of the batman as  that meant reeves though had to forge  ahead without his leading man he chose  to do this in a way that would both  honor batman's long past and push him to  new and different heights and reeves and  craig would have to be the ones to take  him there in the wake of ben affleck's  leaving the project matt reeve's goal  was to present a batman who would be  changed completely by the events of the  film reeves told the new york times i  wanted the stakes of the story to  challenge him in a way that shook him to  his core instead of a movie about a  disillusioned wayne forced a face that  his vigilante ways weren't getting the  job done the movie would now center  around quote someone who hadn't quite  figured out why they were doing the  thing they were doing reeves continued  to say that for his version of bruce  wayne he's still stuck in those events  that happened when he was 10. with this  in mind the project zeroed in on a time  period several years into his life as  batman soon enough reeves had his new  batman and robert pattinson a choice  that affleck ultimately approved of  calling pattinson a good actor during an  interview and the rest of the  production's pieces slowly fell into  place it isn't the film that fans would  have seen had affleck still being batman  but it definitely seems to be a worthy  entry  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  batman are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

